     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "The school kept a weather chart with daily temperature and rainfall.\n\"We can see patterns,\" said the teacher."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "thermometer",
     "rain gauge",
     "barometer"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Weather is the day-to-day condition of the atmosphere: temperature, rainfall, wind, humidity and air pressure. It changes often.\nTemperature is measured with a thermometer, rainfall with a rain gauge, air pressure with a barometer and wind direction with a wind vane.\nWarm air rises and makes low pressure; cold air sinks and makes high pressure. Wind blows from high to low pressure."
    }
